---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const cmds = `git clone https://github.com/cikick/cikick && cd cikick
# the 2nd install links the built bins
pnpm install && pnpm build && pnpm install
cd examples/consumer && pnpm exec cikick check`;
---
<section id="quickstart" class="sec sec-alt" aria-labelledby="qs-title">
  <div class="wrap qs">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Quickstart</p>
      <h2 id="qs-title">Build it from source, check a real consumer.</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        This clones the cikick monorepo, builds every package from source, then runs <code>cikick check</code> on
        <code>examples/consumer</code>: a repo that uses a shared package, with its generated <code>ci.yml</code> and
        <code>cikick.lock.json</code> committed. The check verifies they match the config, offline.
      </p>
      <p class="note">
        cikick is pre-release (0.1.0) and its packages are not yet published to a registry, so there is no <code>npm install</code> yet.
        The guide covers wiring it into your own repo.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn" href={`${base}/docs/guides/quickstart/`}>Quickstart guide</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${base}/docs/concepts/constructs-and-synth/`}>How synth works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="code-win term-win">
      <div class="win-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>terminal</b>
        <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="qs-cmds">Copy</button></div>
      <pre class="code qs-pre" id="qs-cmds" tabindex="0">{cmds}</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
